## Waves that slide in from the left. Self-contained (no import).
##
## The profile is a 46-tube wave followed by a 16-tube blank gap (period 62).
## Scrolling it rightward (reverse=true) means new content enters from the left:
## the gap clears the screen, then the waves slide in from the left, cross, and
## exit right into the next gap. Loops forever with no jump because the gap makes
## the loop point an empty screen.

title|Waves slidein
scale|0.12
loop|forever

sprite|b0|0x0000
sprite|b1|0x0008
sprite|b2|0x0808
sprite|b3|0x0888
sprite|b4|0x0889

segment|crest_1|{b1}
segment|crest_2|{b1}{b2}{b1}
segment|crest_3|{b1}{b2}{b3}{b2}{b1}
segment|crest_4|{b1}{b2}{b3}{b4}{b3}{b2}{b1}

## 46-tube wave + 16-tube blank gap = 62-tube period.
segment|wave_profile|{b0}{crest_1}{b0}{crest_3}{b0}{b0}{crest_2}{b0}{b0}{crest_4}{b0}{b0}{crest_2}{b0}{b0}{crest_1}{b0}{crest_4}{b0}{crest_2}{b0}{crest_1}{b0}{b0}{b0}{16}

sequence|start|wave_window
frame|1|{wave_profile}{wave_profile}
sequence|end
## shift=-(period-16) = -46 starts the loop on the empty gap, so the animation
## opens with the slide-in instead of part-way through the wave.
sequence|insert|wave_window|shift=-46|repeat=62|shift_step=-1|reverse=true
